keywords:
  - cryptography
  - key-derivation-function
  - n-body-simulation
  - chaos-theory
  - post-quantum
  - rust
abstract: "Kelvin is an experimental cryptosystem that derives cryptographic keys from the chaotic evolution of an n-body gravitational system. It combines Q32.64 fixed-point arithmetic, symplectic Verlet and Euler integrators, Lyapunov time estimation, SHAKE256 entropy extraction, and multiple encryption modes including ChaCha20Poly1305 (V1), SHAKE256 XOR streaming (V2), HKDF-SHA512 batch OTP (V3), and hybrid quantum streaming (H)."
